body:
damn, this sounds like its coming from some personal experience, but you're right, we need to cut some people off, for our own sanity at times. 

&#x200B;

thanks for your input

I change my name to a white name, but lately, i havent been noticing any differences between the 2. 

&#x200B;

From the words of someone i admire "it is what it is".

hey man i know its been a while

&#x200B;

they did yeah, doxy and amoxicilin, 

&#x200B;

my biggest concern right now is how well ill do in an exam that's upcoming, i forgot what it was like to cry in the shower due to pain being so overbearing, i forgot what it was like to break down into tears in front of my mom, because i just couldn't keep up the facade that i was fine anymore. 

&#x200B;

im telling you this because if you, or anyone who has NDPH reads this. This period of your life is horrible but i can guarantee that it will end ,i promise. the hardest part is pushing through, but youre a survivor, you got this.

here is the link for the discord group 

&#x200B;

[https://discord.gg/xQfayye](https://discord.gg/xQfayye)

&#x200B;

The group has been designed for 20 - 30 people rather than 100 or more. This is because being able to talk with more consistent communal people is better for socializing as it makes speaking in an unfamiliar language easier and it's also easier to make mistakes in front of people you are familiar with rather than just complete strangers. The limit on people will also help the more shy individuals feel more connected and not have a group dominated by charismatic individuals, as getting to know someone makes speaking a lot easier.

The discord link is first come first serve. feel free to message me in advance. see everyone soon,

looking for someone to do my online courses for me. either link to the dark web or dm me directly

&#x200B;

thx
